{
  "id": "stokes__formula",
  "title": "Stokes' Formula",
  "description": "Viscosity force acting on a smooth sphere.",
  "type": "datatable",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Stokes' Formula\n\nThe force of viscosity acting on a smooth sphere in stream line motion can be expressed with Stokes' formula:\n\n**F = 6 π η r v** (1)\n\nWhere:\n- **F** = force (N)\n- **η** = viscosity of fluid (Pa·s)\n- **r** = radius of sphere (m)\n- **v** = relative velocity between fluid and sphere (m/s)"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "viscosity",
          "label": "Viscosity (η)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "Pa·s",
          "defaultValue": 0.001
        },
        {
          "id": "radius",
          "label": "Radius of sphere (r)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "m",
          "defaultValue": 0.001
        },
        {
          "id": "velocity",
          "label": "Relative velocity (v)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "m/s",
          "defaultValue": 1
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "force",
          "label": "Viscosity Force (F)",
          "formula": "6 * 3.14159265 * inputs.viscosity * inputs.radius * inputs.velocity",
          "unit": "N",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Parameter",
        "Symbol",
        "Value",
        "Unit"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Viscosity of fluid",
          "η",
          "inputs.viscosity",
          "Pa·s"
        ],
        [
          "Radius of sphere",
          "r",
          "inputs.radius",
          "m"
        ],
        [
          "Relative velocity",
          "v",
          "inputs.velocity",
          "m/s"
        ],
        [
          "Viscosity Force",
          "F",
          "6 * 3.14159265 * inputs.viscosity * inputs.radius * inputs.velocity",
          "N"
        ]
      ]
    }
  ]
}